{
    "//1": "Category 3: CDN (domain) fronting - restricts to the FRONTED-MEEK-* protocol",
    "//2": "family, where traffic is an HTTPS connection to a real CDN edge that then",
    "//3": "relays to the actual Psiphon server (see README's 'Improving DPI resistance'",
    "//4": "section for how FRONTED-MEEK differs from TLS-OSSH/plain meek).",

    "//5": "IMPORTANT - read before using this file:",
    "//6": "1) As of the vendored commit in psiphon-core/ (see VENDOR_COMMIT), a client CANNOT",
    "//7": "   invent its own fronting domain via config (there is no such field in",
    "//8": "   psiphon-core/psiphon/config.go - e.g. 'FrontedMeekDialOverrides' and the",
    "//9": "   protocol name 'FRONTED-MEEK-CDN-OSSH' do not exist anywhere in this source;",
    "//10": "   a config using them loads without error but silently does nothing / matches",
    "//11": "   zero candidates, because unknown JSON keys are ignored (see README) and an",
    "//12": "   unrecognized protocol name in LimitTunnelProtocols just filters out every",
    "//13": "   server entry. The fronting domain/host actually comes from each SERVER",
    "//14": "   ENTRY's MeekFrontingHost/MeekFrontingDomain fields (see common/protocol/",
    "//15": "   serverEntry.go) - it's server-side data, not a client-side override.",
    "//16": "2) Checked directly against server-list-standard.txt (391 real entries): ZERO",
    "//17": "   currently support any FRONTED-MEEK-* protocol. This file is here ready for",
    "//18": "   when/if that changes (a server list from Psiphon Inc. that includes fronted",
    "//19": "   entries, or a self-hosted psiphond placed behind your own CDN-fronted domain",
    "//20": "   - the VPS/Cloudflare setup we paused). Until then, launching with this file",
    "//21": "   will just sit at zero candidate servers and never connect.",

    "PropagationChannelId": "07D1ACD69B3AC7A2",
    "SponsorId": "EE0B7486ACAE75AA",

    "LocalHttpProxyPort": 8082,
    "LocalSocksProxyPort": 11080,

    "LimitTunnelProtocols": [
        "FRONTED-MEEK-OSSH",
        "FRONTED-MEEK-HTTP-OSSH",
        "FRONTED-MEEK-QUIC-OSSH"
    ],

    "EmitDiagnosticNotices": true
}
